# SHT: Shift T register - Non-contiguous mask instruction
# YAML: mask "1111_1001_1000_0000", opcode "0154000" (octal)
# Shift operations on T register with multi-shift flag
#
# Performs various shift operations on T register:
# - Arithmetic left/right shifts
# - Logical left/right shifts
# - Rotate left/right with/without carry
#
# Every shift places last discarded bit in multi-shift flag (M).
# M flag (bit 8 of STS register) can be input for next shift.
#
# P-code implementation (example for arithmetic right shift):
# local shift_count:1 = shift_counter & 0x1F;
# local last_bit:1 = 0;
# for (i = 0; i < shift_count; i++) {
#     last_bit = T & 1;
#     T = T s>> 1;
# }
# STS[8,8] = last_bit;  # Set multi-shift flag
#
# SLEIGH Limitation: Cannot implement due to non-contiguous mask
# Pattern "1111_1001_1000_0000" has gaps that cause conflicts
# Manual implementation would require complex sub-table hierarchy